 "notes": "MiniBooNE dump-mode (1.86e20 POT on steel dump) 2-sigma exclusion on g_agamma from Fig. 7 (crimson 'MiniBooNE Dump' contour), extracted from the vector figure MB_ARGONEUT_photon_limits2sigma.pdf in the e-print, calibrated on the axis tick labels. The Lagrangian (Eq. 1) is -(g_agamma/4) a F Ftilde, matching the canonical convention. The excluded region is a wedge: points run from m=1e3 eV along the lower exclusion boundary up in mass to the tip at m~1.8e8 eV, then back along the upper boundary (short ALP lifetime ceiling), which leaves the top of the plotted axes (g~4e-4 GeV^-1) at m~9e6 eV; so the list is a contour trace, not single-valued in mass. The paper also bounds g_ae (Fig. 8) but that MiniBooNE limit lies inside existing lab bounds; the photon coupling is the headline new-parameter-space result (Sec. V). ArgoNeuT curves (3/20/100 events) are projections and are not reported. Beam-dump limit: no dark-matter density assumption.",
